"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1535,"We have Bundar, we have Abu Bakr, meaning the Hanafi, we have Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, Shurahbil, who is Ibn Saad Abu Saad, told me, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray the Maghrib prayer, so I came to him and stood beside him to his left. He discouraged me, so he placed me on his right. Then a companion of mine came, and we lined up behind him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer in one garment, in a different manner. ""between its two ends"""
